# SHA-256 of every upstream file this SDK ships unmodified from the official
# Lua 5.5.1 release tarball.
#
#   https://www.lua.org/ftp/lua-5.5.1.tar.gz
#   released 2026-07-24, 398643 bytes
#   sha256 1c4b4068d67061f2a2231ad2b5422e77acea1487ea9890f6320af614f4373dce
#
# 75 records, 1416954 bytes after extraction: README, Makefile, doc/ (10 files)
# and src/ (63 files). That is the complete file list of the tarball, so a
# dependent receives the upstream project rather than a hand-picked subset of
# it. Nothing is dropped for size and nothing is dropped for being uncompiled:
# the two upstream Makefiles, the manuals, the man pages and the images travel
# even though the Zig build reads only src/*.c.
#
# The tarball carries no test suite -- src/Makefile's `test` target only runs
# `lua -v` -- so no test file is expected here and none is fetched to make one.
# See UPSTREAM.md, "There is no upstream test suite in the tarball".
#
# `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` from the repository root checks the bytes.
# tools/check-provenance.sh additionally rejects a missing, extra or renamed
# file under doc/ or src/, which a plain checksum run cannot see.
#
